WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.840
What would you trade in order to make your
deepest desires a reality?

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.450
How much would you be willing to barter in
order to have what you want?

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:14.519
Whether it’s money, love, fame, or power
that you crave, would you bargain your soul

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:15.559
to have it?

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:17.540
How about your memories?

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.110
What about the life of another person?

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.990
If these questions intrigue you, then boy,
do we have the deal of a lifetime for you!

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:32.730
Well, not us, but rather a certain anomaly
who’s very interested in the art of the

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.730
deal.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.050
We’ve all heard the old adage of a “deal
with the devil”, meaning a pact with someone

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.530
potentially shady in order to get what you
want.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:46.019
Not only are you compromising your own principles
when you make a deal like this, you’re also

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:50.469
running the risk of that deal coming back
to haunt you when it’s time to pay the devil

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:51.930
his dues.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.500
And believe us, the devil always comes to
collect.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.729
Of course, you’ve never made a deal with
the actual Devil, and if you had, it’s likely

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:03.710
you wouldn’t live long enough to warn people
not to make the same mistake.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.500
But we’ve all heard the legends: Beelzebub
appearing to those in dire need of help and

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.409
offering them salvation.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:14.979
Shaking that outstretched, clawed hand normally
results in the desperate person getting what

00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:20.000
they need, but also agreeing to give Satan
something along the lines of their soul or

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.830
firstborn child.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.340
Or sometimes something even worse.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.340
The point being, that dealing with the devil
often extracts a heavy price, and one you

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.060
might not be so willing to pay if you could
see the terms more clearly.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:39.539
Which brings us to SCP-738, also known as
“The Devil’s Deal.”

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:45.009
Although this SCP has no relation to the actual,
biblical Lord of Darkness himself - as far

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.539
as we know, anyway - that nickname should
paint a very clear picture for you of how

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:52.119
this entity operates.

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:58.020
Kept in three linked containment chambers,
SCP-738 is guarded at all times by armed Foundation

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.280
personnel when not in use.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.570
Strangely for an anomaly with such a terrifying
reputation, it appears as an elegant three-piece

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:11.340
set of furniture, the kind you might find
in a fancy office belonging to a slick CEO.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.540
The set consists of a desk, one straight-backed
chair and another, more extravagant office

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:22.920
chair styled to look like a throne, all featuring
brass detailing and exquisite velvet padding

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.200
in a deep, royal purple.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.260
When kept apart, these objects seem to be
little more than just expensive pieces of

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.470
office furniture.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:35.730
Examples of quality craftsmanship that would
likely cost you an arm and a leg to afford,

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.780
but nothing overtly sinister or anomalous.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.420
Until, that is, the three pieces are put together,
and you take a seat.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:47.680
If someone sits down opposite the throne,
with the desk between them, then they had

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.290
best be ready to bargain, because once you
sit down, you will find yourself faced with

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.230
an anomalous entity across from you in the
throne.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.410
While many of the D-Classes the Foundation
have placed before this entity have described

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.060
it as being “charming”, or even “seductive”,
descriptions of the entity’s appearance

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.040
varies wildly between subjects.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:11.450
In fact, it would seem that the entity deliberately
appears differently to everyone that sees

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:16.780
it - their very own personalized devil with
which to strike a deal.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.900
After all, this business is personal.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:23.930
Additionally, the entity cannot be observed
by anyone except for those sitting in the

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.060
anomalous chair of SCP-738.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.520
For anyone not sitting in the special chair,
the most they’ll see of the entity is the

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.409
throne shifting as it leans backwards or sits
up.

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:40.020
It isn’t interested in being seen by anyone
who isn’t part of the transaction.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.340
This entity is clearly quite the negotiator,
and doesn’t waste any time in getting to

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.550
the meat of the conversation.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.709
During tests by the Foundation, recordings
have been made of the entity’s voice, making

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:55.379
all manner of enticing offers and promises
to whomever is sitting before it.

00:03:55.379 --> 00:04:00.110
The entity will produce parchment from the
desk, writing up what looks to be a contract

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.989
with a quill and ink pot.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:06.660
If whoever is sitting in the opposite chair
makes a formal request to the entity, it will

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:12.860
cease its previous barrage of offers and take
a brief pause, before suggesting a price.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:18.120
During their first attempt to gauge the nature
and effects of SCP-738, the Foundation sent

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:23.220
one of its researchers into a room containing
the desk, throne, and chair.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.780
According to his report, he saw a man sitting
behind the desk, wearing a sharp, red and

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.590
gold colored business suit.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:34.250
The entity immediately bombarded the man with
potential deals they could strike, offering

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:39.550
him greater recognition and respect for his
research, the love of the woman the man wanted,

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:44.000
and even offered him the chance to join the
O5 Council.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.430
Refusing to be coerced into any of these deals,
the researcher left the room, and seemed to

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.650
suffer no adverse effects for his refusal.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:57.080
Since this initial incident, when testing
the behavior and effects of SCP-738, the Foundation

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.930
primarily uses D-Class personnel.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:04.750
As we all know by now, these personnel are
considered disposable, having been recruited

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:11.860
from prisons around the world, and ones testing
SCP-738 are fitted with an explosive collar…

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:12.949
just in case.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:19.330
In one instance, one of these Class-D personnel
placed before the SCP-738 entity reported

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:24.830
that this time it had taken on the appearance
of a beautiful, seductive woman.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:30.530
During the initial proposals made by the SCP-738
entity, the inmate was offered his freedom.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:35.340
The price of freedom is often high, but the
Class-D may not have been expecting the price

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.910
to be the death of his best friend.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.670
But the inmate agreed to the terms of the
deal he’d been offered, and vanished shortly

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:42.670
after.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:46.520
Five hours later though, he was recaptured
by Foundation personnel.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:51.510
When another member of Class-D personnel,
a non-native English speaker, sat down to

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:56.599
bargain with SCP-738, the entity communicated
with him in his first language.

00:05:56.599 --> 00:06:01.620
Their deal, while similar to the previous
test, used more specific wording.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:06.300
The Class-D inmate asked for the power to
never be held in a cell again, rather than

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.060
just “for freedom.”

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:13.800
The price asked for by the SCP-738 entity
this time was every memory of the man’s

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.800
mother.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.169
After he accepted, an incident broke out which
resulted in the inmate’s death, as well

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:21.849
as that of twelve Foundation guards.

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:27.150
The next test the Foundation conducted into
the effects of SCP-738 involved yet another

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:32.720
Class-D, this time utilizing an inmate with
dyslexia and a mental disability, who reported

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.770
that the entity appeared to take the form
of a large pink rabbit.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:41.419
Once again adapting to the subject before
it, the entity drew crude pictograms on its

00:06:41.419 --> 00:06:45.970
parchment, trying to convey a deal to the
latest Class-D to sit across the desk from

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:46.970
it.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.830
There were a few words scattered about the
page in English, but mostly unrelated insults

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:56.670
aimed at the inmate’s intelligence, or questioning
the man’s understanding of the deal the

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.370
entity was proposing.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:04.680
The entity offered the man a Sloppy Joe, stating
the price to be ”Mopsy”, the name given

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:10.180
to a toy that the inmate had smuggled into
the Foundation and been allowed to keep.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:14.780
Upon accepting the deal, a fine china plate
appeared in front of the man, with the promised

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.270
sandwich upon it.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:20.410
The man quickly finished the food that the
entity had provided, only to become distressed

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.419
when he realized that Mopsy had vanished.

00:07:23.419 --> 00:07:27.979
Shortly after the test had concluded, Foundation
staff issued the Class-D with another toy,

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:31.150
identical to the one that had been bargained
away from him.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:37.030
However, as soon as he named the new toy Mopsy,
it too disappeared, once again causing the

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:40.440
inmate a great deal of emotional distress.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:45.550
Further testing found that there was little
that could damage the furniture of SCP-738.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:50.280
Foundation researchers even tried exposing
it to explosives, to no effect.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.979
Despite appearing to be crafted from mahogany,
neither the desk nor the chairs were able

00:07:54.979 --> 00:07:56.759
to catch fire and burn.

00:07:56.759 --> 00:08:01.360
Gunshots did not tear through the woodwork
as one would expect, and even a mechanical

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.900
wood chipper did nothing to cause even the
slightest of damage.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.520
There was however, one thing that did.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:13.009
When directly attacking the desk with an axe,
a single gash was left scored into the mahogany

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:15.470
surface by the bladed head.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:20.870
This did, unfortunately, lead to the death
of the personnel wielding said axe, and afterwards

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:24.540
the mark left in the desk began gradually
healing.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:29.080
Changing their approach, the Foundation ceased
sending Class-D personnel to make deals with

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.650
whatever devil appeared sitting at the desk.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:36.770
Instead, a researcher took the seat opposite,
and before the entity began its usual stream

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:41.670
of offers to fulfill deep desires, the researcher
asked a simple question.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.800
“What are you?”

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.780
The SCP-738 entity took the form of a huge
snake, and answered “I'm sorry.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.040
It's against policy to divulge personal details.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.010
But may I interest you in…”

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.840
It is unknown what the entity offered the
researcher, but the session was called to

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:03.280
be halted shortly after, and the Foundation
researcher was institutionalized pending psychiatric

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:04.280
review.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:09.830
The final test of SCP-738 involved a Mr. Sheldon
Katz, senior counsel of the Foundation’s

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:14.690
legal department, who presented the entity
with a fully, legally watertight document

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:20.060
stating he was not acting on behalf of the
SCP Foundation, and was testing SCP-738 of

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:22.670
his own free agency.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:29.090
Mr Katz reported that, in this instance, the
SCP-738 entity assumed the form of a professor

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:34.260
who had taught Sheldon during his first year
of law school, but didn’t include any information

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:38.070
as to what sort of deal the entity had offered
him.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:42.630
After forty-one hours of debate, during which
a nine-hundred-page long agreement between

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:50.290
him and SCP-738 was drafted, Mr Katz eventually
passed out from sheer, overwhelming exhaustion.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:54.950
A red leather envelope was found on him when
he was removed from the testing room, containing

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.000
a handwritten note and smelling heavily of
sulfur.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.910
The note simply read “Please come back any
time.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.410
I haven't had so much fun in years.”

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:09.700
The incidents involving SCP-738 all follow
a strikingly similar pattern.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:14.001
After adjusting to the person before it, both
appearing in a form specific to them, and

00:10:14.001 --> 00:10:20.090
communicating with them in a such way that
they will best understand, the SCP-738 entity

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:24.100
will attempt to entice their latest emptor
with their deepest desires.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:29.650
When the person opposite them makes a request,
the entity brings up the question of price.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:34.540
While they can be negotiated with, it will
insist that the price be of “equal value”

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.410
to what is being requested.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:40.220
Like for like, perhaps even a soul for a soul.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:44.360
It is worth noting that the entity sat in
the throne will not always follow through

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:50.210
on deals if they determine the person making
the request ”does not want the object enough”,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.460
or if they request an object for someone else
as a way of trying to dodge paying the full

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:55.650
price.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:11:00.710
It seems that this entity, being the bargainer
that it is, does not indulge requests that

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:06.920
are made to affect other people, or for items
that can be easily passed on to others.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:11.260
Accepting a deal with whatever devil appears
across that desk from you will make your wish

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:12.260
come true.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:15.190
Isn’t that how deals with the devil always
go?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:20.130
After all, you are certain to get whatever
you ask for, anything your heart desires,

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:23.700
if you’re willing to pay the right price
for it.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.550
Just make sure that you read the fine print
of that agreement before you sign, because

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:32.480
the price won’t always be something you’re
willing to pay.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:39.631
Now check out “SCP-1879 - Indoor Salesman”
and “SCP-662 - Butler’s Hand Bell” for

00:11:39.631 --> 00:11:43.440
more anomalies that’ll make you an offer
you can’t refuse.

